          "detected_by": "stage1_llm",
          "local_context": "# The Fee Plan Changes Overnight, but Oil Prices Still Haven’t Gone Home\n\nThe show begins. The main thing to watch this time is that the fee plan was replaced by a different one the next day, but worries about supply stayed on stage. A quick change in policy alone was not enough for the market to feel safe and bring the curtain down. It did not turn out to be such a simple story.\n\nThe U.S. president posted a proposal to charge a 20% fee on every shipment passing through the Strait of Hormuz, to repay the United States for the cost of keeping the route safe. The label to put up here is not “Already in effect,” but “Proposal.” The fee had not actually been put in place. What had appeared was a proposal.",
