          "detected_by": "stage1_llm",
          "local_context": "So, how did the market respond? After the announcement, Brent futures’ gains shrank for a while, but they soon returned to a high level close to where they had been before it. At the time the article was published, they were up about 2.6%, above $85 a barrel. Worries also continued about attacks between the United States and Iran, the naval blockade, and the safety of tankers.\n\nThe fee plan has left the stage. But worries about supply will not stay hidden in the wings. For the market, this did not seem to be something that could be settled by a quick change in a post alone. The curtain seemed about to fall, but it did not. That is what makes this news interesting.\n\n## In one line\nTrump quickly replaced his proposed Hormuz shipping fee, but oil prices stayed high amid continuing supply worries.",
